WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.362
The dangers, and the guard for each.

2
00:00:02.362 --> 00:00:06.854
A CRL that grows past the limit
takes down every card from that CA,

3
00:00:06.854 --> 00:00:10.499
so the size rule and its
early warning run every time.

4
00:00:10.499 --> 00:00:15.375
A slow or unreachable endpoint causes
the same outage from the network side.

5
00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:18.900
A CA without a CRL lets
revoked cards sign in.

6
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.088
A renewed CA nobody added
locks out new cards.

7
00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:26.037
A troubleshooting exemption that
stays turns revocation off.

8
00:00:26.037 --> 00:00:31.075
PIV mapped as single-factor means
the card isn't what meets MFA.

9
00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:34.800
And a report-only policy is
a requirement only on paper.
